    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d300">

                <pb facs="0323" n="314" sameAs="frus:frus1938v05/pg314"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">835.30/44: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in
                        Brazil</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Caffery</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-04-01T18:00:00-05:00">April 1, 1938—6 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>47. Your 75, April 1, noon. Please inform Aranha that this Government is not
                    sending any naval mission to Argentina nor has it been requested to do so. As he
                    knows, three American naval officers <pb facs="0324" n="315" xml:id="pg315"/>
                    have been acting as instructors in the Argentine Naval War College for the past
                    three years.<anchor n="32" xml:id="d300-f1"/></p>
                <p>I believe that the unfounded report he has received is due to the fact that the
                    Argentine Government has requested this Government to lend the services of
                    American instructors in aviation. This Government has agreed in principle to do
                    this but the details have not yet even been discussed. Since this matter is as
                    yet entirely confidential and any premature publicity would be unfortunate, I
                    leave it to your own judgment whether to communicate these facts to Aranha for
                    his strictly confidential information or not.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
